    "blurb": "Local, private AI for Camunda",
    "overview": "Run open-weight AI models locally with Ollama inside Camunda processes, with no cloud API costs, full data privacy, and a native BPMN task powered by a custom Java outbound connector.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Run local AI models inside your processes",
    "splashDescription": "Cloud AI APIs add per-request costs and send prompts outside your infrastructure. This connector lets Camunda processes call locally running, open-weight AI models through Ollama — no cloud AI API and no per-request billing required. The connector sends a prompt from a BPMN process to Ollama's OpenAI-compatible local API (http://localhost:11434/v1), and returns the model's response back into the process. It ships with a Camunda Modeler element template (\"Ollama Chat\") so the task appears natively in the palette, and extends Camunda's official Self-Managed Docker Compose setup (via extra_hosts, LOADER_PATH, and a JAR volume mount) to bridge the connector container to Ollama running on the host — without modifying the official distribution. Supports models such as llama3.2, mistral, qwen2.5, and gpt-oss:20b, keeping all prompts and responses on local infrastructure for full data control and zero per-token cost.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/871407/overview/img15265190083386916757.png?dc647e93abea6562fd489581f4f67582",
    "imageSrcset": {
      "default": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/871407/overview/img15265190083386916757.png",
      "2x": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/871407/overview/img15265190083386916757-2x.png",
